                         Thieves
---------------------------------------------------------------------

Thieves turn information, access, and timing into power. Case a mark,
build Opportunity through meaningful setup, then spend it on dirty
control or a prepared finish. Thieves work in ordinary PvE, parties,
and dual-guild builds: Bleeding and Exposed are the common conditions
used by every guild.

Thief advancement uses Guild XP, not gold. Ranks 1 through 20 open the
command kit; later uncapped ranks support Knacks, diminishing mastery,
and utility progression. Each rank grants one Knack point.

Useful starting commands:

  tstatus                 Current GXP, Opportunity, study, and incident
  knacks                  Ghost, Grifter, and Knife training
  case <target>           Study one mark and create two Opportunity
  quickstrike <target>    Open a canonical Bleeding wound
  dirtyfight <option>     Spend Opportunity on feint, punch, or sand
  sidestep                Spend Opportunity on short evasive footwork
  detect                  Find trap signs and hidden exits
  extract <corpse>        Harvest a poisoncraft reagent
  prepare <poison>        Prepare a persistent dose

Use 'thelp revival' for the complete system overview.
